ht · near the North Gate B-52 display","notes":"Choose the short out-and-back route, stay on the established trail, and use the B-52 parking area and trail amenities as directed.","short_summary":"An easy 1.4-mile trail beginning near the North Gate B-52 static display.","evidence_claim":"Falcon Spur Trail is an easy 1.4-mile out-and-back route that begins near the North Gate B-52 display; the Academy lists parking there plus restrooms, trash cans, and picnic tables.","source_url":"https://www.usafa.edu/visitors/hiking-and-biking-trails/","source_title":"Hiking and Biking Trails","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use daylight and stay on the established path. The Academy requires dogs to be leashed and directs visitors to follow current base-entry instructions.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":["On-base destinations remain subject to Academy entry rules and operational restrictions. The Friday-only Noon Meal Formation and weekday Planetarium option are intentionally conditional rather than assumed weekend activities."]}],"warnings":[]}
