s designated roadside overlook for a broad view of the athletic fields, then continue only on public roads and signed areas.","short_summary":"A self-guided-tour stop overlooking the Academy’s athletic complex.","evidence_claim":"Athletic Overlook is the second overlook along Academy Drive and looks toward 57 athletic fields covering more than 140 acres.","source_url":"https://www.usafa.edu/visitors/self-guided-tour/","source_title":"Self-Guided Tour","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"A drive-up overlook on the official self-guided route; access remains subject to installation entry requirements.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"usafa-doolittle-hall","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Doolittle Hall","title":"Walk the Heritage Trail at Doolittle Hall","subtitle":"Friday daytime · 3116 Academy Drive","notes":"Follow the Heritage Trail across Challenge Bridge and stop at the Southeast Asia Pavilion and Memorial Wall before heading out.","short_summary":"Association of Graduates headquarters with outdoor Vietnam-era memorial exhibits.","evidence_claim":"Doolittle Hall is home to the Association of Graduates; its Heritage Trail includes Challenge Bridge, the Southeast Asia Pavilion, and Memorial Wall.","source_url":"https://www.usafa.edu/visitors/self-guided-tour/","source_title":"Self-Guided Tour","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Official self-guided tour lists parking; the gift shop is open to the public Monday–Friday, 8 a.m.–4 p.m., but purchases are optional.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"usafa-falcon-spur-trail","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Falcon Spur Trail","title":"Make Saturday a Falcon Spur Trail walk","subtitle":"Saturday daylight · near the North Gate B-52 display","notes":"Choose the short out-and-back route, stay on the established trail, and use the B-52 parking area and trail amenities as directed.","short_summary":"An easy 1.4-mile trail beginning near the North Gate B-52 static display.","evidence_claim":"Falcon Spur Trail is an easy 1.4-mile out-and-back route that begins near the North Gate B-52 display; the Academy lists parking there plus restrooms, trash cans, and picnic tables.","source_url":"https://www.usafa.edu/visitors/hiking-and-biking-trails/","source_title":"Hiking and Biking Trails","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use daylight and stay on the established path. The Academy requires dogs to be leashed and directs visitors to follow current base-entry instructions.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":["On-base destinations remain subject to Academy entry rules and operational restrictions. The Friday-only Noon Meal Formation and weekday Planetarium option are intentionally conditional rather than assumed weekend activities."]}],"warnings":[]}
